#+title: CFT-Code
#+auto_tangle: t
#+PROPERTY: header-args:zig :tangle ../../src/cft-code/cft-code.zig :mkdirp yes

The following module is the worldsheet CFT core of the project. It defines symbolic [[id:20260605T082209.767536][Expressions]] used in worldsheet CFT calculations i.e. local [[id:20260603T094125.997360][Operators]] multiplied by nontrivial [[id:20260604T083119.372970][Coefficients]] and computes their [[id:20260603T094112.928043][OPE]] and [[id:20260603T094138.285453][Correlators]]. It can also generate a basis of local operator with a given set of quantum numbers via [[id:20260606T063253.759714][Basis-Generation]]. The data of a CFT or BCFT is defined in [[id:20260605T090102.250727][Theory]], exposed to users through [[id:20260606T163500.000000][Presets]], built by the DSL, and executed by [[id:20260606T150002.000000][CFT Kernel]].

As far as dependencies go, this module only depends on [[id:20260605T075909.433647][Tensor-Code]], which forms an integral part of the definition of [[id:20260604T083119.372970][Coefficients]] and determines the properties of various quantum numbers of [[id:20260603T094125.997360][Operators]]. The module itself only exposes the symbolic [[id:20260605T082209.767536][Expressions]] manipulated by other parts of the code and [[id:20260603T094112.928043][OPE]], [[id:20260603T094138.285453][Correlators]].

#+api:

Export [[id:20260605T082209.767536][Expressions]]
#+begin_src zig
/// expressions exposes symbolic CFT expression data.
pub const expressions = @import("expressions/expressions.zig");
/// theory exposes CFT and BCFT specification data consumed by generated kernels.
pub const theory = @import("theory/theory.zig");
/// kernel exposes the generated-kernel data structures used by the DSL.
pub const kernel = @import("kernel.zig");
/// presets exposes physics-facing CFT and BCFT preset constructors.
pub const presets = @import("presets.zig");
#+end_src
